\begin{slide}
Damped Harmonic Oscillator Covariance Analysis
\begin{itemize}
  \item Matrix Riccati Differential Equation with constant $F$, $H$, $Q$, $R$
  \item Varying $R$ demonstrates extreme sensivitiy of $P$ solution to changes in $R$
  \item $R=3.3$ is stable; but $R=3.4$ is unstable
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}

\begin{slide}
Damped Harmonic Oscillator Covariance Analysis
\begin{itemize}
  \item Example illustrates how damping coefficient (reflected in system dynamics matrix) and process noise uncertainty interacts with measurement noise uncertainty
  \
\end{itemize} 
\end{slide}


